---

## 📈 Tableau Dashboard

The dashboard provides a visual overview of Flowerama's financial and operational performance.

![Flowerama Tableau Dashboard](dashboard.png)

### Dashboard Components

| Visualization | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Quarterly Profitability | Track changes in profit and loss across quarters |
| Revenue by Weekday | Compare sales performance throughout the week |
| Revenue by Order Type | Evaluate in-store, online, and delivery contributions |
| Revenue vs. Profit | Compare sales activity and profitability |
| Revenue vs. Expenses | Examine operating performance |
| Wage Expense Analysis | Evaluate labor costs as a share of expenses |

---

## 🔍 Key Findings

| Area | Finding |
|---|---|
| **Quarterly Performance** | The dashboard shows a Q1 loss followed by improved performance in Q2. |
| **Order Channels** | In-store orders account for approximately **43% of total revenue**, as reported in the dashboard. |
| **Weekly Revenue** | Sunday generated substantially less revenue than other operating days. |
| **Operating Costs** | Wages account for approximately **24% of expenses**, according to the dashboard. |
| **Profitability** | Revenue and expense comparisons reveal changes in financial performance across reporting periods. |

---

## 💡 Business Impact

The project demonstrates how retail businesses can use financial reporting and data visualization to:

- Identify underperforming sales periods.
- Understand which order channels contribute to revenue.
- Monitor operating expenses and profitability.
- Support more informed staffing and operational decisions.

The findings were presented at the end of the semester, connecting financial analysis with practical business considerations.

